.TH CHERUBSH 1 "August 2026" "CherubSH" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
cherubsh \- a Bash-compatible shell for Linux and WSL
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B cherubsh
[GNU long option] [option] ...
.br
.B cherubsh
[GNU long option] [option] script-file ...
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B cherubsh
is a Rust implementation of Bash 5.3 behavior. It runs commands from a string,
a script file, standard input, or an interactive terminal. Bash is not required
at runtime.
.PP
CherubSH is tested on glibc-based Linux and WSL. Official archives target
.B x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu
and
.BR aarch64-unknown-linux-gnu .
On a different Linux ABI, build from source; those environments are not part of
release testing. Keep the system Bash installation in place because
operating-system scripts may depend on the distribution build.
.SH LONG OPTIONS
.TP
.BR --debug , " " --debugger
Enable debugging behavior. The debugger form also enables debugger mode.
.TP
.B --dump-po-strings
Extract translatable strings in PO form without executing the input.
.TP
.B --dump-strings
Extract translatable strings without executing the input.
.TP
.B --help
Print invocation help and exit.
.TP
.BR --init-file " path", " " --rcfile " path"
Read an alternate interactive startup file.
.TP
.B --login
Request login-shell startup behavior.
.TP
.B --noediting
Disable line editing in an interactive shell.
.TP
.B --noprofile
Skip login startup files.
.TP
.B --norc
Skip the interactive CherubSH startup file.
.TP
.B --posix
Enable POSIX mode.
.TP
.B --pretty-print
Parse and print shell input without executing it.
.TP
.B --restricted
Start in restricted mode.
.TP
.B --verbose
Print input as the shell reads it.
.TP
.B --version
Print the CherubSH package version, Bash compatibility version, and target.
.SH INVOCATION OPTIONS
.TP
.BI -c " command"
Run a command string.
.TP
.B -s
Read commands from standard input.
.TP
.B -i
Force interactive operation.
.TP
.B -l
Request login-shell startup behavior.
.TP
.B -r
Enable restricted mode.
.TP
.B -D
Extract translatable strings without executing input.
.TP
.BI -O " shopt-option"
Enable a shell option before startup. Use a plus prefix to disable it.
.PP
The Bash-style short shell options
.B -abefhkmnptuvxBCEHPT
and
.BI -o " option"
are also accepted.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.cherubrc
Startup file for an interactive, non-login CherubSH shell.
.TP
.I ~/.bash_history
Default interactive history file when HISTFILE is not set.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B CHERUBSH_BASH_COMPAT_VERSION
Overrides the displayed Bash compatibility version when the value can be
parsed as a version number.
.TP
.B BASH_ENV
Names a startup file for a non-interactive shell when the current mode permits it.
.TP
.B ENV
Names the startup file used by POSIX or sh-compatible interactive modes.
.SH EXIT STATUS
The exit status is the status of the last command, or a nonzero status for an
invocation, parsing, expansion, or execution error.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR cherubsh-readline (3),
.BR cherubshrc (5),
.BR bash (1)
.SH BUGS
Report defects and Bash compatibility mismatches at
https://github.com/cupidthecat/cherubsh/issues.
